A. Status: optional, no longer needed for MOTRES's own distribution
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Not yet effective, and -- after the architecture decision above -- no
longer required for MOTRES's own default server image or default
distribution, which as of this revision do not contain Intel MKL, any
Intel MKL component, or `pypardiso` at all. This permission is kept in
the repository, in DRAFT, for a narrower purpose: `pypardiso` remains an
optional, user-installed, user-enabled backend (an operator's own
`pip install pypardiso` plus their own MKL, never installed or enabled
by MOTRES's own build or deploy process) for anyone who wants PARDISO's
speed on their own infrastructure. Recommendation: keep this permission,
scoped to that optional path, rather than delete it -- see Section D for
why an operator who self-installs MKL still benefits from MOTRES having
granted it. When cleared by counsel, MOTRES d.o.o. will date this file
and it will apply, from that date, to every version of the Program in
this repository (github.com/eMotres/Motor_Ai_Simulation) from the commit
at which this file was first added onward, until withdrawn or superseded
by a later dated version of this file.

